   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The composite has outer function F with \\( \\frac{d}{du} \\sqrt{u} = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} \\) and inner function \\( u = 25 - x^{2} \\), whose derivative is \\( - 2 x \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "identify the layers"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule and the chain rule, \\( h'(x) = - \\frac{2 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{25 - x^{2}}} + 4 x \\sqrt{25 - x^{2}} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "product rule with the chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = -3 the inner value is 16 and the inner derivative is 6, so \\( h'(-3) = -48 + 18 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot 6 = - \\frac{69}{2} \\).",
